Advance Correction Slio No.9 to Indian Railwavs Standard General Conditions of
ContrecL
ril2022
A. Para 16.(4), Part II ofGCC-2022 shall be read as under:-
f6.(4) PerformanceGuarantee
The procedure for obtaining Performance Guarantee is outlined below:(a) The successful bidder shall have to submit a Performance Guarantee (PG) within 2l(Twenty one) days from the date of issue of [rtter of Acceptance (LOA). Extension of timefor submission of PG beyond 2l (Twenty one) days and upto 60 days Aom the date of issueof LOA may be given by the Authority who is competent to sign the contract agreement.However, a penal interest of l2o/o per annum shall be charged for the delay beyond2l(Twenty one) days, i.e. from 22dday after the date ofissue ofLOA. Further, if the 60fidayhappens to be a declared holiday in the concemed oflice of the Railway, submission of PGcan be accepted on the next working day.In ail other cases, if the Contractor fails to submit the requisite PG even after 60 daysfrom the date of issue of LOA, the conhact is liable to be terminated. [n case contract isterminated railway shall be entitled to forfeit Bid Security and other dues payable to theconfactor against that particular contract, subject to maximum of PG amount. In case atenderer has not submifted Bid Security on the strength of their registration as a Startuprecogr.ized by Department of Industrial Policy and Promotion (DIPP) under Ministry ofCommerce and Industry, DIPP shall be informed to this effect.The failed Contractor shall be debarred from participating in re-tender for that work.
(b) The successfirl bidder shall submit the Performance Guarantee (PC) in any of thefollowing forms, amounting to 5% of the original contract value:-(i) A deposit of Cash;(ii) Irrevocable Bank Guarantee;(iiD Insurance Surety Bond as per Annexure-XVII.Note:l. The provision oflnsurance Surety Bond shall be for all contracts havingDOC within 36 months only.2. In case DOC extends beyond 36 months, fresh Insurance Surety Bond orany other form of Performance Guarantee prescribed in GCC for thebalance amount shall be submitted by agency, otherwise necesary actionwill be taken as per terms of Agreement.
(i") Govemment Securities including State Loan Bonds at 5% below the market value;
